3.2 (Multiple machines.) You may install and use the Software on multiple computers for your own use (or, where you accept on behalf of an entity, for that entity's internal use).

3.3 (Internal distribution.) Distributing the unmodified installer internally to your own personnel for their use under this Agreement is permitted and is not a prohibited redistribution under Section 4.

3.4 (Stability of the version you hold.) For so long as you comply with this Agreement, the license granted in this Section for the specific release you have installed remains in effect for that release, and is not retroactively revoked, repriced, or converted to paid terms by anything the Licensor does with respect to a later release (including charging for it). New terms apply only when you obtain or update to a release offered under those new terms (Section 9).

