6. Your responsibilities; connected devices

The Software is a tool that, at your direction, performs actions that affect connected devices and the apps and data on them. You are solely responsible for:

6.1 (Authorization.) ensuring that you own, or are authorized by the owner to access and operate, every device, emulator, and system you connect to or interact with using the Software, and that you have all necessary rights and consents to read its logs and data;

6.2 (User-initiated actions.) every device-affecting action you initiate through the Software — including installing, launching, force-stopping, and uninstalling apps, and accessing logs or data — and all consequences of those actions, including loss, corruption, or unavailability of apps or data, device misconfiguration, and downtime;

6.3 (Backups; compliance.) maintaining appropriate backups, and complying with all laws, organizational policies, and third-party terms applicable to the devices, apps, and data you handle. Some actions (e.g., uninstalling apps, overwriting installed packages) may be irreversible and may result in data loss; you assume full responsibility for such actions.

7. Privacy and telemetry

7.1 The Software's telemetry is optional and opt-in. By default it is privacy-preserving and does not transmit telemetry until you enable it.

7.2 Where enabled, telemetry is limited to minimal crash-reporting data (via Sentry) from which personally identifiable information is scrubbed; you may select off or crash-reports-only, and may disable it at any time. Any processing of telemetry is limited to operating, maintaining, and improving the Software.

7.3 We do not sell your data. Where a separate privacy notice is provided, it supplements this Section.

